  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the maintainer, I want a checked list proving every legacy function exists, so that no user loses a feature in the update.\n\n### Scope\n\nWalk the legacy inventory (screens, settings, actions) against the app on the Mac; each row ends 'ported', 'intentional difference (documented)' or an open issue. No submission here (LOT-165 (#255)).\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: high · post-MVP (App Store release blocker)\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: decomposition goal 'app at legacy parity'; FEATURES 'Not to lose' checklist\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): the legacy inventory table of decomp/app-lots.md\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-164-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-070 (#94, blocked)\n- LOT-081 (#99, done)\n- LOT-083 (#101, done)\n- LOT-084 (#176, done)\n- LOT-085 (#177, done)\n- LOT-086 (#178, done)\n- LOT-087 (#179, done)\n- LOT-088 (#180, done)\n- LOT-089 (#181, done)\n- LOT-100 (#191)\n- LOT-101 (#192)\n- LOT-102 (#193, done)\n- LOT-103 (#194, done)\n- LOT-104 (#195, done)\n- LOT-105 (#196, done)\n- LOT-106 (#197, done)\n- LOT-107 (#198, done)\n- LOT-108 (#199, done)\n- LOT-109 (#200, done)\n- LOT-110 (#201)\n- LOT-113 (#204, done)\n- LOT-114 (#205, done)\n- LOT-115 (#206, done)\n- LOT-116 (#207, done)\n- LOT-117 (#208, done)\n- LOT-118 (#209, done)\n- LOT-119 (#210, done)\n- LOT-120 (#211)\n- LOT-121 (#212, done)\n- LOT-123 (#214, done)\n- LOT-124 (#215, done)\n- LOT-125 (#216, done)\n- LOT-126 (#217, done)\n- LOT-127 (#218, done)\n- LOT-128 (#219, done)\n- LOT-130 (#220)\n- LOT-131 (#221)\n- LOT-132 (#222)\n- LOT-133 (#223)\n- LOT-134 (#224)\n- LOT-135 (#225)\n- LOT-136 (#226, done)\n- LOT-137 (#227, done)\n- LOT-139 (#229, done)\n- LOT-140 (#230)\n- LOT-146 (#236)\n- LOT-155 (#245, done)\n- LOT-156 (#246)\n- LOT-157 (#247)\n- LOT-158 (#248)\n\n### Blocked by\n\ndependencies not done: LOT-070 (#94, blocked), LOT-100 (#191), LOT-101 (#192), LOT-110 (#201), LOT-120 (#211), LOT-130 (#220), LOT-131 (#221), LOT-132 (#222), LOT-133 (#223), LOT-134 (#224), LOT-135 (#225), LOT-140 (#230), LOT-146 (#236), LOT-156 (#246), LOT-157 (#247), LOT-158 (#248)\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every legacy row of the inventory has a verdict and evidence (screen, test or issue).\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
